{"kind":"artifact","text":"Candidate at performance for the retained fan-out evidence, exact head 0f4ab4c30f414827c1461cbc6aa03ed90376eb8f.\n\nGoverned by request e6fcd142 through promise 7045345b. The commit carries Rests-On for e6fcd142 and for e1ab6474, because the same head also publishes the verdict this evidence supports.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, and only this. A tracked directory performance/retained/fanout-20260819-f71b4d73 holding exactly three files, and a rewritten retention section in performance/README.md. performance/.gitignore is untouched; git diff --quiet against main returns identical. git ls-files performance/retained/ returns exactly three paths and nothing else, which I checked after the final amend rather than after the first attempt.\n\nWHY THIS EXISTS. A run writes into performance/evidence, ignored working space inside the worktree, and step 6 of the working discipline deletes that worktree after merge. The previous fan-out campaign went that way: its digests are still quoted in the log and its page still told readers the medians must not replace the distributions, but the distributions were gone. This retains the run the published verdict is derived from before the same thing happens again.\n\nTHE THREE FILES, with digests I recomputed at this head rather than carrying forward: evidence.json 61a53e96c9bf31da07d7e37722d5bd2225f4f5ea9dad5a8bbf2e30acf9254a7b, samples.jsonl 21c74a93ff7ec928297b4fb25196244d1c61529b60b8028abe27f3d1f8ff3209, candidate.bench f5078a0e1263305c3615359c7f558c9ed12df414c3b5fe4da74afd28aa9e93e6. evidence.json is the harness evidence document and retains the harness's own latency distributions and fan-out axis summary alongside the contract, the environment, the fixture and contract digests and the exact head. samples.jsonl holds every raw record, 505 of them: 100 primary per width at 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256, plus one round-zero diagnostic each. candidate.bench holds the 500 primary samples in Go benchmark form. I verified all 500 primary trusted-versus-projected digest pairs equal.\n\nNo separate derived file is retained. An earlier attempt at this work also tracked a notes file, a distributions file and a load log; review found those outside the authorization, and they were also the wrong shape, because the harness's summaries already travel inside evidence.json and any further statistic is recomputable from the samples. What those files carried that mattered was the account of how the run was conducted, and that now lives in docs/reference/performance.md where it is reviewed rather than sitting unread beside the data. The README says this accurately: it does not claim nothing derived is retained anywhere, only that no separate derived file is.\n\nREPRODUCIBILITY, WHICH REVIEW CAUGHT AND WAS RIGHT ABOUT. Because *.bench is ignored, copying the files in and running an ordinary git add silently leaves candidate.bench untracked. The README now gives the exact sequence including git add -f for that one file, and the git ls-files check to confirm the directory holds three files and nothing else, with the reason stated inline: the ignore rules will not tell you what they dropped. Both are text blocks, so no gate executes them. Retention stays a deliberate act on one run whose numbers reach a page.\n\nSECURITY. I scanned all three files for absolute local paths, the operator's username, private key blocks and password or secret-key strings: zero hits in each. Profiles, traces and fixtures are excluded, the first two being diagnostic reruns rather than primary evidence and the third large and regenerable from the contract. Nothing here touches signing, admission, verification, fold semantics or publication; it adds data files and prose.\n\nTHE RUN THESE FILES RECORD. Both harness_commit and candidate_commit are f71b4d73c46b5df1ba2c755571fc8ffdf4455275, read from evidence.json rather than assumed equal; that commit is this head's parent. Contract digest b0795bc7..., recomputed through perflane.CorrectnessDigest from a contract file byte-identical to main's. One fixture exact digest d15f714d throughout. Clean worktree, Darwin arm64 on an 18-core Apple M5 Max, Go 1.26.5, Git 2.50.1. One process invocation, exit 0.\n\nIt is the second complete campaign. The first was suspended by machine sleep partway through width one and discarded whole rather than partly repaired, because the records carry no wall-clock timestamp and a spanning suspend cannot be found in them afterwards. The retained population is entirely the rerun. Width one and width eight both moved across their own blocks and machine load was observed rising during the run; the page reports those observations without asserting that either caused the other, since load was sampled only at twenty-second intervals and no sample can be aligned to the machine's state when it was taken.\n\nHISTORY. This head's ancestry was rebuilt so that nothing outside the five authorized paths is reachable from the branch at all. A later deletion would not have made those blobs unreachable, so the branch is two commits: f71b4d73, the measured commit, and this one. Every path touched across the whole ancestry is one of the five.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD, each tool's own exit code captured directly: gofmt 0 unformatted, go build 0, go vet 0, go test -count=1 ./... 0 across 26 packages with zero failures, docset uncached at 62.137 seconds. Tree clean; local and origin both at this commit; merge-base with origin/main is 92dd2df1 itself.\n\nPredecessor at this path is 4da5ebd0, live, not stale and not describes_superseded_world when I checked immediately before publishing. Retirement belongs to the merge, not here. I have not merged.","body":{"commit":"0f4ab4c30f414827c1461cbc6aa03ed90376eb8f","path":"performance"}}